sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as coordinator
  participant S as SchedulerEngine
  participant D as Disk (SCAN)
  participant M as MemoryEngine
  participant P as PipeEngine

  Note over C: one simulated tick

  C->>S: tick()
  activate S
  S->>S: admit arrivals onto the least-loaded CPU
  S->>S: count down self-timed I/O waits
  S->>S: priority boost / load balance
  S->>D: submit(pid) when a CPU burst ends on an I/O burst
  D-->>S: accepted — process goes WAITING(disk)
  S-->>C: what each CPU ran this tick
  deactivate S

  C->>D: advanceTick()
  D-->>C: requests the head serviced
  C->>S: wake(pid, 'device') for each waiter

  loop for each busy CPU
    C->>M: access(page)
    M-->>C: fault / eviction / copy-on-write
    C->>P: stepEndpoint(pid)
    P-->>C: transferred, or must block
    C->>S: blockOn(pid,'pipe') or wake(counterpart,'pipe')
  end
